Find $\tan Y$ in the right triangle shown below.

[asy]
pair X,Y,Z;
X = (0,0);
Y = (24,0);
Z = (0,7);
draw(X--Y--Z--X);
draw(rightanglemark(Y,X,Z,23));
label("$X$",X,SW);
label("$Y$",Y,SE);
label("$Z$",Z,N);
label("$25$",(Y+Z)/2,NE);
label("$24$",Y/2,S);
[/asy]

Solve the problem step by step. At the end, write the final answer inside \boxed{}.

What is the value of $x$ in the plane figure shown?

[asy]
pair A;
draw(dir(40)--A); draw(dir(200)--A); draw(dir(300)--A);
label("$160^{\circ}$",A,dir(120)); label("$x^{\circ}$",A,dir(250)); label("$x^{\circ}$",A,dir(350));
[/asy]

Solve the problem step by step. At the end, write the final answer inside \boxed{}.

In right $\Delta ABC$, $\angle CAB$ is a right angle. Point $M$ is the midpoint of $\overline{BC}$. What is the number of centimeters in the length of median $\overline{AM}$? Express your answer as a decimal to the nearest tenth. [asy] pair A,B,C,M;
A = (0,0); B = (4,0); C = (0,3); M = (B+C)/2;
draw(M--A--B--C--A);
label("$A$",A,W); label("$B$",B,E);
label("$C$",C,W); label("$M$",M,NE);
label("3 cm",A--C,W); label("4 cm",A--B,S);
[/asy]

Solve the problem step by step. At the end, write the final answer inside \boxed{}.

The isosceles triangle and the square shown here have the same area in square units. What is the height of the triangle, $h$, in terms of the side length of the square, $s$?

[asy]
draw((0,0)--(0,10)--(10,10)--(10,0)--cycle);
fill((0,0)--(17,5)--(0,10)--cycle,white);
draw((0,0)--(17,5)--(0,10)--cycle);
label("$s$",(5,10),N);
label("$h$",(6,5),N);
draw((0,5)--(17,5),dashed);
draw((0,5.5)--(0.5,5.5)--(0.5,5));
[/asy]

Solve the problem step by step. At the end, write the final answer inside \boxed{}.

For the ellipse shown below, find the distance between the foci.

[asy]
unitsize(0.3 cm);

int i, n = 10;

for (i = -n; i <= n; ++i) {
  draw((i,-n)--(i,n),gray(0.7));
  draw((-n,i)--(n,i),gray(0.7));
}

draw((0,-n)--(0,n));
draw((-n,0)--(n,0));

draw(shift((1,1))*xscale(2)*yscale(6)*Circle((0,0),1),red);

dot((1,1));
[/asy]

